  "headline": "Price of 12kg LPG cylinder increases by Tk 252 in Bangladesh",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "The Bangladesh Energy Regulatory Commission (BERC) announced on October 4, 2026, that the consumer price for private-sector liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) has increased. The price of the most widely used 12kg LPG cylinder rose by Tk 252, moving from Tk 1,585 to Tk 1,837. This represents a price increase of Tk 21 per kilogramme. The new pricing was scheduled to take effect at 6:00 pm on October 4, 2026. This follows a price decrease of Tk 13 during the previous month."
    },
    {
      "text": "The price adjustment follows a period of fluctuation in the international market. While prices declined for two consecutive months in June and July following a ceasefire, a significant surge occurred this month. Previously, in April, the country saw its highest-ever increase in LPG prices, when the 12kg cylinder price rose by Tk 387 at the beginning of the month and by an additional Tk 212 on 19 April. BERC noted that LPG cylinders of various sizes remain available in the market, though allegations have surfaced that 12kg cylinders are being sold at Tk 500 to Tk 800 above the official price due to market supply remaining below demand for the past three weeks."
    }
  ]
}

