  "headline": "Former Ghanaian Ambassador congratulates New Patriotic Party leaders on election results",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Edward Boateng, the former Ghanaian Ambassador to China, has congratulated John Boadu and Justin Frimpong Kodua following their election and re-election, respectively, as National Chairman and General Secretary of the New Patriotic Party (NPP). Following the NPP’s National Delegates Conference, Mr. Boateng stated that the results carry a responsibility for both leaders to rebuild the party, strengthen its structures, and unite members ahead of the 2028 general elections. He urged the new National Chairman to use his mandate to promote reconciliation and bring together members who supported different candidates during the internal elections. Mr. Boateng noted that Mr. Kodua became the first person since Dan Botwe to be elected as General Secretary for a second consecutive term, and stated that Mr. Kodua must work with Chairman Boadu to ensure party structures function effectively from the polling station to the national level."
    }
  ]
}

