  "headline": "Amazon rainforest policy future tied to Brazilian presidential election",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Brazil’s upcoming presidential election may determine the future of the Amazon rainforest, which accounts for approximately 60% of the ecosystem. Experts have warned that a victory for Senator Flávio Bolsonaro, the son of former President Jair Bolsonaro, could reverse deforestation-control policies that were restored by President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva. During the presidency of Jair Bolsonaro, Amazon deforestation increased by about 60%. In 2023, President Lula reinstated an anti-deforestation plan that reduced deforestation by 45%. Flávio Bolsonaro has pledged to end illegal deforestation by 2029, though he has not provided details on how this goal would be achieved. Concerns persist regarding the potential weakening of environmental protections."
    }
  ]
}

